articles.content_en:
Article 1: First-instance foreign-related civil and commercial cases shall be under the jurisdiction of the following People's Courts:
(1) the People's Courts in the economic and technological development zones approved by the State Council;
(2) the Intermediate People's Courts located in provincial capitals, capitals of autonomous regions, and municipalities directly under the Central Government;
(3) the Intermediate People's Courts of special economic zones and cities under separate state planning;
(4) other Intermediate People's Courts designated by the Supreme People's Court; and
(5) Higher People's Courts.
The territorial jurisdiction scope of the above-mentioned Intermediate People's Courts shall be determined by the Higher People's Courts of their respective localities.

Article 3: These Provisions shall apply to the following cases:
(1) foreign-related contract and tort dispute cases;
(2) letter of credit dispute cases;
(3) cases applying for setting aside, recognition and compulsory enforcement of international arbitral awards;
(4) cases for examination of the validity of arbitration clauses concerning foreign-related civil and commercial matters; and
(5) cases applying for recognition and compulsory enforcement of civil and commercial judgments and rulings of foreign courts.
